# sanskrit

## संस्कृतलिपि

Verum Script is a Lisp, so every word can be Sanskrit. परिभाषा is define,
अस्तु is let, आह्वानम् is call - the only thing a program can do to the world.
Type it on a Latin keyboard with `lipi on`: paribhASA becomes परिभाषा.

```
(परिभाषा (सन्देशे प्रेषकः विषयः)
  (अस्तु ((वस्तु (आह्वानम् भाण्डारः "प्राप्" विषयः)))
    (आह्वानम् पटलः "मुद्रय" "शब्दाः" (परिमाणम् (विभज (गृहाण वस्तु "data") " ")))))
```

This page carries a cell: the Sanskrit word counter. It asks to read the
store and print. Nothing runs until you say `allow`, and then it can do
exactly that and nothing else - it will count the words of this very page.

@cell ganana store[get,put] console[print]

